<title>UK: Camargo Correa plans $150 mln bond-dealers.</title>
<headline>Camargo Correa plans $150 mln bond-dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian construction group Camargo Correa plans to launch a $150 million Eurobond this month, bankers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The deal was expected to have an eight-year maturity with puts and calls after five years. Chase was tipped as lead manager.</p>
<p>Emerging market debt specialists said the bond could surface as early as next week.</p>
<p>Camargo Correa's core businesses are construction and engineering, and recently it has also invested in Brazil's cement industry.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
